scraplinux-base is hand-written, not generated from manifest.tsv: its
package() copies the whole skel/ and branding/ trees out of the committed
skel.tar/branding.tar, which the generic meta template cannot express.
gen-ports.py overwrote it once with the generic stub (source="", no
package()), which silently turned scraplinux-base into an empty package -
this file is what stops that happening again.

Regenerate the tars with build/gen-skel-tar.sh before every release. They
are frozen archives, so every skel/ fix is invisible to a real install
until that is run and this package is rebuilt and republished.
